sweet 0110 (u-tr): SWEET_TU_CPUPROF=1 - where Turnip's CPU time goes, for CA's frames. Times (os_time_get_nano, atomics
across threads) vkCmdDrawIndexed, its state emission (tu6_draw_common) and the consts+descriptor part of that,
vkCmdBindPipeline / BindDescriptorSets2 / PushConstants2, vkCmdBeginRenderPass2 / EndRenderPass2 (and tu_cmd_render in
it), vkCmdExecuteCommands, vkBegin/EndCommandBuffer and new command-stream BOs (tu_cs_add_bo: kernel alloc + map), and
counts draws that re-emitted all state / changed program / had dirty consts / dirty sets. Exported
sweet_tu_cpu_report() gives "<name> calls/mean us/total ms ..." since its last call (SweetMetal2 logs it every 5 s as
"native-metal: T tu-cpu:"). Off by default: one relaxed load per entry point.
